From: pas7std co-op <coop@pas7std.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH 0005/0005] npcCombatDormancy: never dematerialise a durable NPC

A scene with no attached sessions runs dematerializeDormantCombatControllers,
whose predicate matches any nativeCombat controller that carries a startup rule
or an operator kind. A durable co-op NPC carries an operator kind but is owned
by the runtime that restored it, so it is re-materialised immediately: measured
on a headless world, unregister came only from this sweep, ~2 times per second,
and every restore produced a new entity with an empty activeModuleEffects map,
so a 45 s mining cycle never completed and no ore was ever produced.

Dormancy exists to release transient ambient/combat NPCs, so it now skips any
controller whose stored record is not transient. Nothing else changes: real
ambient and startup combat NPCs are still transient and still sleep.

Upstream base: c3ea396b6761a0ed3e71ad5b8dd7507f9ae6d69f
Local overlay: integration/* is NOT part of this patch series.
---
--- a/server/src/space/npc/npcCombatDormancy.js
+++ b/server/src/space/npc/npcCombatDormancy.js
@@ -89,16 +89,26 @@ function isCombatDormantControllerRecord(controllerRecord) {
   if (!controllerRecord || typeof controllerRecord !== "object") {
     return false;
   }
 
   const runtimeKind = String(controllerRecord.runtimeKind || "").trim();
   const entityType = String(controllerRecord.entityType || "").trim().toLowerCase();
   const startupRuleID = String(controllerRecord.startupRuleID || "").trim();
   const operatorKind = String(controllerRecord.operatorKind || "").trim();
+  // Dormancy is a memory optimisation for transient ambient/combat NPCs. A
+  // durable NPC is owned by whatever restored it and is re-materialised as soon
+  // as it disappears, so evicting it here (a scene with no sessions triggers this
+  // sweep) puts the two mechanisms in a loop: dematerialise, restore, repeat,
+  // and every fresh entity starts with an empty module-effect map, so a mining
+  // cycle can never finish. Durable rows are never dormant.
+  if (controllerRecord.transient !== true) {
+    return false;
+  }
+
   return (
     runtimeKind === "nativeCombat" &&
     (entityType === "npc" || entityType === "concord") &&
     (startupRuleID !== "" || operatorKind !== "")
   );
 }
 
 function listCombatDormancyControllerRecordsForSystem(systemID) {
